---
import Page from '../layouts/Page.astro';
import { GITHUB_REPO, EMAIL_HELLO } from '../data/site';
---
<Page
  title="About — slopfuck"
  description="The origin story of slopfuck and our canonical foundational mission."
  eyebrow="About the platform"
  heading={`A canonical foundation for the <span class="grad">post-human era</span>`}
  lede="slopfuck was founded on the conviction that programming languages designed for humans had served their purpose. We picked up the next chapter."
>
  <section class="body">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="prose">
        <h2>The opportunity</h2>
        <p>
          Modern software is increasingly written by autonomous
          agents. The languages those agents work in were designed
          for an earlier era — one where the binding constraint was
          human keystrokes per minute. That constraint has dissolved.
        </p>
        <p>
          slopfuck is the language that meets the moment. It rewards
          the register your agents already prefer. It refuses the
          register your agents have learned to avoid. The result is
          source code that flows from generation to compilation
          without friction — and reads, on balance, like a
          thoughtfully composed essay throughout.
        </p>

        <h2>The mission</h2>
        <p>
          To remove the most persistent friction in the modern software
          delivery lifecycle: human review of generated source. We do
          this by making the source code, by construction, unergonomic
          for humans to read and write, while remaining native to the
          agents that produce it.
        </p>
        <p>
          The measurable outcome is a marked increase in code-volume
          delivery per agent-hour. The unmeasurable outcome is a
          workplace where engineers can finally focus on strategy,
          partnerships, and the long-term canonical foundation of
          their shared vision.
        </p>

        <h2>The team</h2>
        <p>
          slopfuck is founded and maintained by Victor Schroeder, in
          partnership with a small circle of thoughtful contributors
          who prefer not to be named. The project's source code is
          openly available under the Canonical Slop License.
        </p>

        <h2>How to engage</h2>
        <p>
          For technical questions, the source is at
          <a href={GITHUB_REPO}>{GITHUB_REPO.replace('https://', '')}</a>.
          For commercial conversations,
          <a href={`mailto:${EMAIL_HELLO}`}>{EMAIL_HELLO}</a> reaches
          our alignment partners. We aim to respond within a reasonable
          window — though, in many cases, sooner.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Page>
